 `collection.diagnostic` is an optional read-only diagnostic for the latest local Claude, Codex or xAI collector invocation. It contains `attempted_at` (UTC timestamp), `provider`, `response_received` and `json_valid`. Claude includes `five_hour`; Codex includes `primary_window` and `secondary_window`. Each field object contains only booleans: `present`, `null`, `quantity_null`, `quantity_valid` and `five_hour` (the field represents a five-hour window; for Codex its reported duration is 18000 seconds). Explicit zero is valid without a reset; absent or null quantities remain unknown. No response bodies, quantities, reset values or credentials are included.
 
-For xAI, `xai.monthly.fields` and `xai.weekly.fields` contain only fixed schema paths and `present`, `null` and `numeric` flags. Numeric means a finite representation accepted by the quota parser, including numeric strings and one `val` wrapper. Wildcard product paths report any presence/null and require every product value to be numeric. `xai.phase`, `vendor_call_started`, `probe_finished`, `snapshot_write_attempted` and `snapshot_persisted` distinguish a forced claim refusal, an HTTP client attempt and a saved or refused completion. `attempted_at` is the Home collector invocation time, never the SDK request or a retained failure time. Scheduled claim refusals do not replace a completed probe diagnostic.
+For xAI, `xai.monthly.fields` and `xai.weekly.fields` contain only fixed schema paths and `present`, `null` and `numeric` flags. Numeric means a finite representation accepted by the quota parser, including numeric strings and one `val` wrapper. Wildcard product paths report any presence/null and require every product value to be numeric. `xai.phase`, `vendor_call_started`, `probe_finished`, `snapshot_write_attempted` and `snapshot_persisted` distinguish a forced claim refusal, an HTTP client attempt and a saved or refused completion. `attempted_at` is the Home collector invocation time, never the SDK request or a retained failure time. Scheduled claim refusals do not replace a completed probe diagnostic. The optional profile diagnostic reports only the fixed subscription-tier field/type flags. On an eligibility parsing failure, `xai.profile.failure_reason` is one of `malformed`, `missing`, `ambiguous`, `non-string` or `unknown-tier`; it never includes the tier value or profile payload.
 
 The diagnostic is available before stdout logging completes and retains one latest attempt per live credential. It is process-local and omitted until a supported collection attempt, after a Home restart, or for other providers. `attempted_at` identifies the diagnostic attempt independently of the saved quota snapshot; it does not assert that the snapshot write succeeded. This field is detail-only and does not initiate a collection.
 
